@startuml status_list_encoding

'=== Settings ===
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
    BorderColor #555555
    FontSize 13
}
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam ranksep 40

rectangle STV #AliceBlue [
    **Status values** (example: capacity 8, bits 2)
    |= idx |= 0 |= 1 |= 2 |= 3 |= 4 |= 5 |= 6 |= 7 |
    | Status | VALID | INVALID | SUSPENDED | VALID | INVALID | INVALID | VALID | SUSPENDED |
    | Value | 0 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 2 |
]

rectangle SBA #OldLace [
    **Status byte array** (ceil(capacity × bits / 8) = 2 bytes)
    |= Byte |= Bit 7-6 |= Bit 5-4 |= Bit 3-2 |= Bit 1-0 |= Value |
    | 0 | idx 3: 00 | idx 2: 10 | idx 1: 01 | idx 0: 00 | 0x24 |
    | 1 | idx 7: 10 | idx 6: 00 | idx 5: 01 | idx 4: 01 | 0x85 |
]

rectangle ZL #WhiteSmoke [
    **ZLIB compression** (DEFLATE, level 9)
    78 DA 53 69 05 00 00 CF 00 AA
]

rectangle LST #Honeydew [
    **status_list.lst** (base64url without padding)
    eNpTaQUAAM8Aqg
]

STV -down-> SBA : write the value of idx i\nat bit position i × bits
SBA -down-> ZL : compress
ZL -down-> LST : encode

note right of SBA
    Byte position: floor(i × bits / 8)
    Bit position within the byte (shift): (i × bits) mod 8
    Lower indexes are in the lower bits (LSB first).
    Unwritten indexes have the value 0.
end note

note right of LST
    Status value check (verifier):
    raw = zlib.decompress(base64url_decode(lst))
    value = (raw[bit // 8] >> (bit % 8)) & ((1 << bits) - 1), bit = idx × bits
    e.g. idx 7: bit 14 → byte 1, shift 6 → (0x85 >> 6) & 0x3 = 2 (SUSPENDED)
end note

@enduml
